{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent non-author three-stage review: APPROVED.\n\nReviewed exact source commit 013767c7f1ebb4b4ec151f25098d8a4e954d12fb against immutable basis 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e. The three immutable blobs are byte-identical at the commit parent 665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732.\n\nStage 1 — Spec Compliance: PASS.\n- AC1 PASS: exactly the ten allowlisted prose blocks and adjacent blank lines changed across the three declared paths; no executable or unlisted prose change was found.\n- AC2 PASS: independently recomputed normalized executable AST equality and exact directive/shebang inventory equality for all three immutable/final blobs.\n- AC3 PASS: each receipt row below records the preserved export/import, batch-resume, diagnostic, or leaf-scheduling contract after direct before/final and consumer comparison.\n- AC4 PASS for this comments-only change under the operator CI waiver: 30 non-benchmark focused cases passed; the unchanged 3,000-record benchmark again reached pytest’s built-in 300-second per-test timeout while creating records, with no assertion failure. Executable AST identity excludes this prose-only patch as its cause. Comment hygiene, path-scoped diff integrity, commit-ticket validation, and worktree-venv make lint all passed. Full make verify is deferred to Gerrit CI.\n- AC5 and AC6 PASS: the receipt contains exactly ten unique, fully cited rows; every row records both PASS verdicts and strict shrink.\n- AC7 PASS with the same transparent timeout disposition and CI waiver described above.\nArchitecture Compliance: PASS against AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, and ADR 0078. The unchanged runtime tree preserves the rebar._io boundary, importer batching/resume contracts, JavaScript-safe export seam, and container-versus-leaf scheduling rule.\n\nStage 2 — Code Quality: PASS. Every replacement is current-state focused, materially shorter, and clearer while retaining its governing invariant. No over-build, test weakening, or recurring review suggestion was found.\n\nStage 3 — Domain Integrity: PASS / not applicable. No executable AST, identifier, type, validation, state representation, or domain boundary changed; primitive-obsession and bool-as-state checks found no introduced issue.\n\nREVIEW_RESULT: {\"per_stage\":[{\"stage\":\"spec-compliance\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"findings\":[]},{\"stage\":\"code-quality\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"findings\":[]},{\"stage\":\"domain-integrity\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"findings\":[]}],\"overall_verdict\":\"APPROVED\",\"required_changes_count\":0,\"blocking_findings_count\":0}\n\nReview persistence is on this leaf rather than a new .reviews path: the exact three-path contract forbids adding another tracked file, and AGENTS.md makes the ticket the durable record.\n\nReceipt word rule: (?u)\\b[\\w][\\w’'-]*\\b; totals 864 -> 247.\n\nstable_block_id\tbefore_citation\tfinal_citation\tpreserved_contract_or_consumer\tdirectives_exact\tbefore_words\tafter_words\tsemantic-preservation\tbloat-removal\treviewer_session\ntests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py#D:<module>\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L1-L18\t013767c7f1ebb4b4ec151f25098d8a4e954d12fb:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L1-L8\tPytest export/import interface retains the RFC 8259 safe-range premise, js_safe_dumps decimal-string wire form, canonical-int import, deterministic HLC premise, and exact-digit checks.\tPASS\t170\t60\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments/review-717a\ntests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py#C:<module>:before:_HLC_INEXACT_BASE_NS\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L37-L45\t013767c7f1ebb4b4ec151f25098d8a4e954d12fb:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L27-L28\tThe ns_ticket fixture retains REBAR_HLC_NOW injection and a 256-aligned base whose next two HLC ticks exceed 2**53 and are float64-inexact.\tPASS\t103\t20\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments/review-717a\ntests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py#C:<module>:inline:_HLC_INEXACT_BASE_NS\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L46\t013767c7f1ebb4b4ec151f25098d8a4e954d12fb:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L29\tThe assignment annotation retains the 256 alignment and two float64-inexact successor invariant.\tPASS\t8\t5\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments/review-717a\ntests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py#D:ns_ticket\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L85-L95\t013767c7f1ebb4b4ec151f25098d8a4e954d12fb:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L68-L72\tThe fixture retains deterministic HLC injection plus JavaScript-safe-range and float64-inexact precondition checks.\tPASS\t82\t22\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments/review-717a\ntests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py#D:test_ns_ticket_timestamps_are_deterministically_float64_inexact\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L169-L178\t013767c7f1ebb4b4ec151f25098d8a4e954d12fb:tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:L146\tThe dedicated regression test retains deterministic above-safe-range and float64-inexact requirements.\tPASS\t87\t10\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments/review-717a\ntests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py#D:<module>\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py:L1-L16\t013767c7f1ebb4b4ec151f25098d8a4e954d12fb:tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py:L1-L6\tThe int